      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Eagles Mere Historic District was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1996.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagles_Mere%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Visitors once rode a narrow‑gauge railroad from Sonestown up the mountain to Eagles Mere.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.happeningsmagazinepa.com/2023/06/30/eagles-mere-a-long-and-storied-history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The kidney‑shaped Eagles Mere Lake covers 230 acres and stretches about three‑quarters of a mile long.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.happeningsmagazinepa.com/2023/06/30/eagles-mere-a-long-and-storied-history/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "From the 1880s to the 1940s, five large resort hotels, including the Forest Inn opened in 1902, lined the lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagles_Mere%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
